  "summary_en": "EESC own-initiative opinion on how digitalisation and AI affect the liberal professions in the EU. It stresses trust, data protection, human-in-command, transparency, updated training and adapted professional self-regulation, with legislation only where self-regulation fails. It has no robotics content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "AI must remain under 'human in command'; final decisions rest with people",
   "AI should be human-centred and transparent, with the same liability standards as other services",
   "Professional self-regulation and codes of conduct should be adapted to digital developments, with legislation as a fallback",
   "EU should fund digital skills training and secure digital infrastructure",
   "Encourage new professions in line with the Rome Manifesto"
